      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E.4",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        347.32196044921875,
        86.9239730834961,
        356.1687316894531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Model architectures for the objective function",
      "bbox": [
        97.8828353881836,
        347.32196044921875,
        307.65533447265625,
        356.1687316894531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our objective function J takes as input future action proposals at:t+F −1 and future states st:t+F , and regresses",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        367.63092041015625,
        540.0429077148438,
        379.0875244140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the discounted future reward as defined in Eq. (2). We again implement our objective function J using a",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        379.5859069824219,
        540.0103149414062,
        389.54852294921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "transformer, using the same transformer layer as in Appendix E.1. We project all states and actions to a",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        391.5408935546875,
        540.2174682617188,
        401.5035095214844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "shared token space with tokens of dimension 256, and specify an additional learnable token for the discounted",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        403.49591064453125,
        540.2405395507812,
        413.4585266113281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "future reward. We add Fourier positional embedding with 16 Fourier bases to all tokens, pass all tokens",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        415.4508972167969,
        540.217529296875,
        425.41351318359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "through a transformer of 10 layers, take the token that corresponds to the discounted future reward, and",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        427.4059143066406,
        540.2278442382812,
        437.3685302734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "read out the discounted future reward prediction. We train the objective function J using an L2 loss.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        439.3619079589844,
        514.634521484375,
        449.32452392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In our experiments for all domains except Hopper, we used a discount factor of 0.99. For Hopper we used a",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        457.2939147949219,
        540.21484375,
        467.25653076171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "discount factor of 0.997. For Walker2D and Hopper, episodes can terminate early due to the agent falling",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        469.2489013671875,
        540.2122192382812,
        479.2115173339844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "down. For episodes that terminate early, we include an additional −100 termination penalty for the last step",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        481.20489501953125,
        540.0772094726562,
        491.1675109863281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as reward, and calculate the discounted future reward taking into account the termination penalty.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        493.159912109375,
        503.9284362792969,
        503.1225280761719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E.5",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        519.4039306640625,
        86.9239730834961,
        528.250732421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Training setups and hyper-parameters",
      "bbox": [
        97.8828353881836,
        519.4039306640625,
        270.1561279296875,
        528.250732421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all of our model training, we use the Adam optimizer for which the learning rate warms up from 0 to",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        539.7119140625,
        540.0008544921875,
        549.6744995117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "10−4 over 500 steps and then follows a cosine decay schedule from 10−4 to 10−5. We train all models for",
      "bbox": [
        71.50199890136719,
        547.85693359375,
        540.243408203125,
        561.6304931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2 × 106 steps. We use gradient clipping at norm 5, and uses EMA with a decay factor of 0.99. All of our",
      "bbox": [
        71.7509994506836,
        560.0068969726562,
        540.3895263671875,
        573.5855102539062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "evaluations are done using the EMA parameters for the models.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        575.577880859375,
        351.2815246582031,
        585.5404663085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E.6",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        601.8219604492188,
        86.9239730834961,
        610.6687622070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Compute Resources",
      "bbox": [
        97.8828353881836,
        601.8219604492188,
        188.19381713867188,
        610.6687622070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We train and evaluate all models on A100 GPUs. We use a single A100 GPU for each training run, and",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        622.1309204101562,
        540.1871337890625,
        632.093505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "separate worker with a single A100 GPU for evaluation. Training for 2 × 106 steps for each variant takes",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        630.4699096679688,
        540.0625,
        644.0485229492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "about 2 days, for all variants we considered.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        646.0408935546875,
        264.1187744140625,
        656.0034790039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "F",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        673.7530517578125,
        79.30462646484375,
        684.3693237304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hyper-parameters for the sampling-based planner",
      "bbox": [
        92.4553451538086,
        673.7530517578125,
        363.09722900390625,
        684.3693237304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all of our experiments, we use a forecast horizon F = 32, number of samples N = 64, and a history",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        697.9808959960938,
        540.392333984375,
        707.9434814453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "length H = 1. A forecast horizon F = 32 already works well since our trained objective function J predicts",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        709.9368896484375,
        540.03173828125,
        719.8994750976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "discounted future rewards.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        721.8919067382812,
        187.665771484375,
        731.8544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "19",
